        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/c/d07c76/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2017-07-14T17:25:56.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Am I missing something, or is Bugbear not damaging himself from Blood Scent at the start of his turn if it's in his play area? &nbsp;In most situations, this would not change much, as he would then gain as much HP as damage he dealt. &nbsp;However, this does make a difference when regaining HP is affected, with cards like Phosphorecent Chamber, Unhallowed Halls, or Oprressive Smog. &nbsp;Regardless of the result, we should still see Bugbear attacking himself, as that is the rules as written on the cards.</p><p>Blood Scent says:</p><blockquote><p><span data-sheets-userformat=\"{&quot;2&quot;:15041,&quot;3&quot;:[null,0],&quot;9&quot;:0,&quot;10&quot;:1,&quot;12&quot;:0,&quot;14&quot;:[null,2,0],&quot;15&quot;:&quot;calibri,arial,sans,sans-serif&quot;,&quot;16&quot;:11}\" data-sheets-value=\"{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:&quot;At the start of Bugbear's turn, Bugbear deals the target next to this card 3 melee damage unless one player discards 2 cards.\\nThen, move this card to Bugbear's play area.&quot;}\">At the start of Bugbear's turn, Bugbear deals the target next to this card 3 melee damage unless one player discards 2 cards.<br>Then, move this card to Bugbear's play area.</span></p></blockquote><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:49:42.706Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
