        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>Am I missing something, or is Bugbear not damaging himself from Blood Scent at the start of his turn if it&#39;s in his play area? &nbsp;In most situations, this would not change much, as he would then gain as much HP as damage he dealt. &nbsp;However, this does make a difference when regaining HP is affected, with cards like Phosphorecent Chamber, Unhallowed Halls, or Oprressive Smog. &nbsp;Regardless of the result, we should still see Bugbear attacking himself, as that is the rules as written on the cards.</p><p>Blood Scent says:</p><blockquote><p><span data-sheets-userformat=\"{&quot;2&quot;:15041,&quot;3&quot;:[null,0],&quot;9&quot;:0,&quot;10&quot;:1,&quot;12&quot;:0,&quot;14&quot;:[null,2,0],&quot;15&quot;:&quot;calibri,arial,sans,sans-serif&quot;,&quot;16&quot;:11}\" data-sheets-value=\"{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:&quot;At the start of Bugbear's turn, Bugbear deals the target next to this card 3 melee damage unless one player discards 2 cards.\\nThen, move this card to Bugbear's play area.&quot;}\" style=\"font-size: 110%; font-family: calibri;\">At the start of Bugbear&#39;s turn, Bugbear deals the target next to this card 3 melee damage unless one player discards 2 cards.<br />Then, move this card to Bugbear&#39;s play area.</span></p></blockquote><p>&nbsp;</p>",
